<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbas III</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abbas III was an infant Safavid shah placed on the throne by the general Nader in 1732 as a nominal ruler. Real power lay entirely with Nader, who deposed him in 1736 and proclaimed himself shah at an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughan-assembly">assembly on the Mughan plain</a>. His removal formally ended Safavid rule and marked the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbas-iii.jpg" alt="Abbas III" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gulustan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbas_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
